        <mxCell id="c70" value="&lt;i&gt;The query as Exercise 13.1 builds it, with the Queries pane at the left. Outlined: the Changed Type step, whose entry for FreightAmount is the decimal number type, and the FreightAmount header with its icon. The grid is scrolled to its left edge; the columns to the right of FreightAmount are out of view, and the freight of these early invoices is whole dollars (Power Query types a column from its first 200 rows).&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="312" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
